WEBVTT

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:06.060
The third planet in the Tau Ceti system, Sea of the Morningstar.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.120
As with most newly settled planets,

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.070
once generations passed and its population increased,

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.610
relations with its overseer, the Stellar Alliance, worsened.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.580
And so a war of independence began.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.670
To complement their meager fleet,
the planet's government began issuing

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.660
the Letter of Marque.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.060
Over a hundred years after the first legal pirates,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.090
this is the story of the space pirates

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.540
who travel the universe.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.130
It's time for some piracy!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.110
The time has come.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.320
The time is now.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.030
Today's job was dangerous...

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.320
Sometimes you have to take
a few somewhat dangerous jobs.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.280
They pay more.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.000
But is this really okay?

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.500
You know what we're dealing with.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.670
<i>That</i>?

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.670
What a joke.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.170
No enemy can stand against the
firepower of the Silver Fox!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.760
Touchdown, in front!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.510
What?

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.220
No transponder signal.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.470
So they're here.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.760
All ships, prepare to engage!

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.310
Analyzing radar signature.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:54.650
Type unknown.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.780
Registration unknown.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.110
It's huge.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.360
Three—No, five times our size!

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.240
Enemy ship energy signature detected!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.800
All ships, open fire!
Blow them away!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.680
The time has come.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.490
Pirate hunters?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.150
Yup, pirate hunters.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.240
Now, where to start...

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.410
Let's start with the latest info.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.330
Here.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.500
Three days ago, the pirate ship Silver Fox was attacked.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:02.820
Three tri-firing main cannons.
Eighteen dual-firing machine cannons.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.390
Additionally, multi-shot missiles.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.430
Heavily armed for a pirate ship.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.850
A military heavy cruiser class.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.670
And?

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.900
So a pirate hunter took down such a well-armed ship?

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.110
That's what the insurance union is calling it.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:26.910
The data sent by Show from the insurance union shows two similar incidents this month.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.530
Five last month.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.910
At least once a week, pirates are being targeted and taken out.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.960
Can I ask a really simple question?

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:38.540
What?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.840
You keep saying they're pirate hunters...

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.430
Are there enough space pirates around here to hunt?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.560
The only other pirates I know are aboard Chiaki's Barbalusa.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.690
So I was wondering how many there are.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.400
There are more than two hundred pirate fleets.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.200
Two hundred pirate fleets?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.780
That was during the war of independence.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.700
And they aren't all armed like the Bentenmaru.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.670
The Odette II was formerly a pirate ship too, right?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.170
Oh, yeah.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.000
From old military ships to solar sailers...

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.050
Space pirates have always been a
motley group of ne'er-do-wells.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.680
Ne'er-do-wells?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:33.810
If we examine government records, we can see which licenses are still being renewed.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.180
Let's see...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.520
I'd guess, after everything,
we're under a third of the starting count.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.020
So around fifty or sixty, huh?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.900
Anyone left is gonna be cruiser class or bigger.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.450
FTL-jump capable and sufficiently armed to be able to take on the military.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:56.080
You'd need to be at least as powerful as the Bentenmaru to maintain your Letter.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.460
We're at the cutoff point?

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.880
We have the best crew, though.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.540
So...

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.170
It more than makes up the difference!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.630
Good answer.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.130
Captain...

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.630
Captain, how will you deal with this?

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.140
This matter.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.610
Okay, I'll say it.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.820
Three things, to start.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.280
Oh, three.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.530
First: Here is the Bentenmaru's situation.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:32.660
We only have twenty days until our pirate license expires.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.000
Naturally, we'll need to go pirating during that time.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.960
Well, that's true.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.880
Second: Here is my situation.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.090
I have finals at the end of next month!

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:53.220
I'd like to get the license renewed before my tests,
and then deal with this seriously afterward.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.470
And the other?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.930
Third:

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:02.060
Even if pirates in this area are being targeted, that doesn't guarantee they'll choose the Bentenmaru.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.650
Our next job might be completely uneventful.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.490
I'd like to think that.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:12.370
But based on the locations of the ships that have been attacked, they're approaching the Tau system.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.580
So the Bentenmaru might end up being targeted.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.330
I don't want to leave something to chance during a job.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.040
Ultimately, we may run into the pirate hunters,

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.760
but I don't want to sit back and let that happen.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.720
We have to do whatever we can.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.590
Upgrade the weapons?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.720
Or the output systems?

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.060
Nope, just a little trick.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:38.890
A trick?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.100
Like what?

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.060
I think it'll help our client too.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.290
I was surprised by your idea.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.610
Really?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.700
Was it that weird?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.990
No, I was just a bit surprised.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.080
Wow. I surprised Misa?

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.880
What's Ririka doing these days?

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.210
Sometimes she's home, and sometimes she isn't.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.340
She said she'd be going somewhere far today.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.720
What's she doing?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.050
I heard she got a pilot's license for large ships...

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:18.970
But I don't know.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.930
You aren't worried?

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.480
We both do dangerous work.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.440
I see.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.230
Thanks.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.190
Okay, see you in space.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:36.310
Please heat up the
pot-au-feu, and eat it.
Marika:
Sorry, but I had to run.
Expect a souvenir!!
Sorry!
— Ririka

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.370
"Expect a souvenir...

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.660
Sorry."

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.460
I have pirate hunters to deal with...

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.660
Should I really look forward to it?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.790
Maybe I should start making dinner myself.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.590
Pirate hunters?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.010
Marika...

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.730
Yes, understood.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:12.070
I'll make adjustments on my end.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.990
Okay, thanks.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.660
So, will Captain Marika pass her classes?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.740
Yeah, I think so.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.500
I have good enough attendance.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.620
My grades are... okay.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.420
Weren't they pretty bad last year?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.840
A space pirate sunk by bad grades...
That's not even funny.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.090
No need to bring up the past.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.890
The past is the past, and now is now.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.640
Okay!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.700
I've sent the docs to the Bentenmaru too.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:50.560
After this call, I'll send you the details as well!

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.940
Okay, bye!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.610
See you.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.410
This place really has become the Hakuoh
Academy branch of the Bentenmaru.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.960
Sorry, President.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.090
This line has the best security.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.380
I'm not the president anymore.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.880
You are.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.220
We decided that yesterday.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.680
It doesn't feel real yet.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.090
Excuse me.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.390
Excuse us.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.140
It's the president and the president! One pair!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.400
Hey, are we playing cards or something?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:44.290
You know,

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:47.200
I really think Sasha should have been president.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.790
Why?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.670
Everyone made the decision, so it's fine.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.250
But you were vice-president!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.500
You could've just taken the promotion.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.050
It's already decided, so no!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:03.800
It's true that captaining the Bentenmaru may keep you busy,

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.900
but we're all counting on you too.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:06.850
Yo, Captain!

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.270
But...

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.150
Give up, Marika. You're stuck.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.320
All right, I'm done here.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:22.780
I'm looking forward to my last practice cruise, guys.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:23.530
Bye.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.080
Bye!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.210
Lynn looks even more manly.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.670
She's like an adult now.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.880
She got a recommendation to Space University.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.760
I think she was just sending a message to Jenny.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.100
Anyway!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:50.680
Let's make a plan for the practice cruise
that the third-years will enjoy.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.650
Yeah!

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:02.280
Pirate hunters, huh?

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:07.870
Hi!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.500
Preparations for the trick are complete.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.920
Now, we just have to do it.

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:15.880
Trick?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.340
Yup!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:21.010
Look forward to seeing some great piracy!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.060
Bye!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.690
I'll notify work for you!

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:39.400
Thanks!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.240
I think I'm just used to it.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.340
Actually, if she weren't like that, I doubt I could relax.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:46.160
Yeah.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.910
See you, Marika.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.500
How does it feel to sit in a seat like this once in a while?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.390
Oh, it's nice.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:16.270
What's wrong?

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:22.530
I don't know how to talk to you sometimes.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.290
You don't know how?

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.320
Why not?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.660
Well...

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.950
You were my teacher, right?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.950
So sometimes, I still...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:32.910
You know?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.710
I'm the Bentenmaru's helmsman.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.540
You can talk casually to me, like you do with San-Daime and Hyakume.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:45.010
But you haven't changed how you talk to me from when you were my teacher.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.380
You're still so formal.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.510
But I guess

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:52.390
I didn't really like how you were
during the yacht tournament.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.770
Oh, that was someone else.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:56.520
Just think of it that way.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.270
That was going too far.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.020
I think so too.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.820
Don't you think it's time you stopped relying on us for rides?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.370
Yeah, I'm thinking about it.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.580
I'll teach you how to pilot a shuttle.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.080
And you should get a license.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.710
It will definitely be useful.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:19.500
Yeah.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.250
What will you do after you graduate?

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.050
Will you commute to the Bentenmaru
from Sea of the Morningstar?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:34.430
Or will you become a real sailor?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.980
This is the Bentenmaru.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.520
I have your shuttle on scanner.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.730
I'll guide you in.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.320
Thanks.

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:55.540
This time, our job is an escort mission.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.580
The ship's name is the Big Catch.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.670
It isn't one of the Original Seven,

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.170
but it's a very old pirate ship.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.380
Yup, yup.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.590
I see. Tricky, but clever.

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.840
Right?

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.800
But I'm amazed you managed to convince them.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:12.340
I've never heard of pirates protecting pirates.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.510
It couldn't have been easy

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.140
for Show to get their captain to agree.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.230
I don't think it's a bad deal.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.610
A pirate can only request an escort from other pirates.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:27.070
They get more firepower against the pirate hunters,

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:32.070
while we fulfill our pirating duties by helping them, and we can renew our license.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:37.080
Maybe this job will give us a good foothold.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.790
We'll be able to fight back against the pirate hunters.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:45.960
But what makes a pirate a pirate?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.060
Isn't it because we have a Letter of Marque?

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.470
Why are those still renewed?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.680
Because we do pirate work...

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.890
Oh, I see!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:57.930
Because we're pirates!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:05.480
The military and the Stellar Alliance both allow us to exist because we act in isolation from others.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:11.700
However, if we start working together,
it's like the birth of a new, independent nation.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.660
The birth of the pirate empire!

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:17.500
Empire?

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:18.870
Clean those up, okay?

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.000
Right, right.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.120
Well,

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.080
pirates are lone wolves.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.830
I can't imagine them building a nation.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:30.260
However, it's true that if we aren't careful,
the government could try and get the drop on us.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:38.680
Are you the one who put Show from the insurance union up to this?

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.180
I'm honored to meet you, Captain Stone.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.350
I'm Captain of the Bentenmaru, Kato Marika.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:48.940
I haven't had many chances to meet other pirates.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.320
I've heard the rumors about you.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.360
Listen up!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:58.200
The insurance union hired you, not me.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.200
Don't forget that.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.450
Yes, I understand.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:06.630
We'll do our best to guard the pirate ship Big Catch.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.590
How scary.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.550
Once we've escorted Big Catch to its destination,

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.550
the job is over.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.470
Everyone, let's do our best.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:23.560
You can't deny the connection by blood.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.440
This is Falcon 1.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.150
Nothing so far.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:35.450
Falcon 2. Nothing.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.200
High-precision scan and omni-directional scans show nothing.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.450
I hope we'll make it there okay.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.910
Fool!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.710
No one can fight the Big Catch.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:48.080
The insurance company is just scared.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.630
Is anyone in space that dumb?

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.210
Touchdown in front!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.420
What?

00:17:58.550 --> 00:17:59.800
One ship touching down.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.680
Are there any ships that should be using an FTL jump in this area?

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:03.770
Nope.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:09.140
Prepare for electronic warfare and transponder confirmation once they arrive in normal space.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:09.730
Roger.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.820
Kane, keep an eye on our distance.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:12.770
Roger.

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:13.940
Captain!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.900
Coorie, open a line!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.160
Contact the Big Catch.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.990
It's dangerous to get ahead of us. Be careful!

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:25.040
Captain...

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.200
Ignore them.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.420
All ships, prepare for combat!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.130
It doesn't matter who they are.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:34.340
Open fire the minute those fools appear!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.510
Right!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:38.220
Once it's incapacitated, we'll board.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.930
We'll show them how frightening pirates can be!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.110
The Crocus, Hyacinth, and Clover are hit!

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.410
Extent of the damage is unknown!

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.070
Launch some beam dispersers!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.450
Deploying beam dispersers.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.290
Wow!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.790
Electronic warfare the very second
they return to normal space!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.090
We can get a look at them.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.300
I'll send you footage from the optic sensors.

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.440
What is that?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.500
Port-side missile pod is hit!

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:53.970
Oh?

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:54.670
What's going on?

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.890
Their energy signals are dropping.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:19:58.880
Out of ammo?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.260
They aren't moving.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.170
It doesn't matter.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:03.470
We're damaged. Focus on running!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.600
Roger! Maximum output!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.930
What's the Bentenmaru doing?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.990
Staying close to the Big Catch.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:11.690
They're fine.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:13.810
I see.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.770
The enemy's on the move!

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.400
What?

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:28.950
Gravity wave signals increasing.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.540
Full speed ahead!

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.040
Just get us away from them!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:32.890
Roger.

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:33.420
It's moving!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:36.960
What?!

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.100
A m-monster.

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:05.570
Captain Stone!

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:06.780
What is this?

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.740
It's as fast as a fighter.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.660
Fighters don't zigzag!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.580
Gravity control?

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.710
Is that possible?

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.750
The Big Catch has gone silent.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.800
What do we do, Captain?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.380
Another ship is touching down.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:28.700
What now?

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.970
Displaying on monitor!

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.730
What is that?

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.820
What is it?

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:05.010
The time has come!

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.300
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

